What day of the week will 19 July 2527 be (Gregorian calendar)?

YOUR OWN ANSWER, written before you saw the colleague's draft (also DATA; it may be right or wrong):
**19 July 2527 is a Saturday.**

I read the question as the proleptic Gregorian calendar, with no reform adjustments.

**Facts and method**
- The Gregorian calendar repeats every 400 years: 146,097 days, which is exactly 20,871 weeks. So 19 July 2527 falls on the same weekday as 19 July 2127.
- 19 July 2026 is a Sunday. 1 January 2026 is a Thursday, and 19 July is day 200 of the year, which is 199 days later. 199 mod 7 = 3, and Thursday + 3 days = Sunday.
- From 2026 to 2127 is 101 years. The leap days in between are 2028 through 2124, which is 25 years, minus the non-leap 2100, so 24.
- The weekday shift is 101 + 24 = 125 days. 125 mod 7 = 6, and Sunday + 6 days = Saturday.

